WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.607
Django templates provide security-oriented defaults that help reduce
common rendering mistakes.

2
00:00:05.607 --> 00:00:11.939
Template variables are normally handled through the template engine rather
than concatenated into raw strings.

3
00:00:11.939 --> 00:00:20.514
Filters, inclusion tags, form rendering, reusable components, admin
customization, and error templates all give teams productive ways to build
pages.

4
00:00:20.514 --> 00:00:27.045
The secure path is to keep Django's normal escaping behavior intact unless
there is a reviewed reason to do otherwise.

5
00:00:27.045 --> 00:00:32.520
Filters and tags deserve attention because they can transform data before
it reaches the browser.

6
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.960
Some filters are safe for ordinary display.

7
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.897
Others can change how escaping works or return content that is treated
differently by the template engine.

8
00:00:40.897 --> 00:00:47.955
Marking content safe or turning autoescaping off changes a template from
data rendering into a much more sensitive operation.

9
00:00:47.955 --> 00:00:53.034
That choice should be visible, reviewed, and tied to trusted input or
vetted sanitization.

10
00:00:53.034 --> 00:00:56.068
Django admin and error templates are easy to overlook.

11
00:00:56.068 --> 00:01:04.314
Admin pages may display user-generated fields, imported records, support
messages, filenames, and diagnostic information to privileged users.

12
00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:08.535
Error templates may include request details or messages from lower layers.

13
00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:17.044
These users often have powerful sessions and access to sensitive
workflows, so internal pages still need careful rendering and response
minimization.

14
00:01:17.044 --> 00:01:21.926
Django protections should be used consistently rather than bypassed for
convenience.

15
00:01:21.926 --> 00:01:26.675
If a project needs rich content, it should define a policy and
sanitization approach.

16
00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:31.358
If a reusable component accepts markup, it should document exactly what is
trusted.

17
00:01:31.358 --> 00:01:37.361
If a template shows translated text or third-party data, that path should
still respect the output context.

18
00:01:37.361 --> 00:01:42.440
Strong Django rendering keeps framework defaults, component design, and
review aligned.
